  "attribute": {
    "SpindleSpeed": "10000",
    "HorizFeed": "100 mm/min",
    "VertFeed": "100 mm/min",
    "RampFeed": "100 mm/min",
    "Stepdown": "0.5 mm",
    "Stepover": "0.2 mm",
    "SourceNote": "Imported 2026-08-17 from vendor/CarveraProfiles/CAM_Post_Processors/Freecad/Tools/bit/Makera_Carvera_M3_Threadmill_Plastic.fctb (Makera 'M3 Threadmill', plastic preset: 400 mm/min, 10000 RPM). HorizFeed here is the TOOL-CENTRE feed for the thread helix: on an M3 the centre orbits at r=0.29 mm, so 400 mm/min at the tooth (Makera's number) is ~77 mm/min at the centre; 100 mm/min is a touch above that. Stepover = radial depth of the first (roughing) thread pass; the second pass goes to full radius. NeckLength 9 mm = usable thread depth (M3 hole < 3.175 shank). Teeth 2 mm from the tip, pitch 0.5, so a continuous helix at 0.5 mm/turn cuts the full thread."
  }
}
